  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LocalizableText.Translated names a language as the name of its set ends, in camelCase: enGB next to ShopTranslationsEnGB, and zhHans next to ShopTranslationsZhHans. It was en_GB and zh_Hans, so rename such arguments. A language without a hyphen keeps its name: nl, fil.\n\nAlso:\n- A language written in upper case in [assembly: SupportedLanguages] gets its parameter in lower case: nl for \"NL\".\n- Two listed languages that differ only in their hyphens, such as sr-Latn-RS and sr-LatnRS, are an error (LOC010): neither a parameter nor the name of a set could tell them apart.",
